# A namespace-qualified global, a::G, given to a ref<T> parameter while a local
# G is in scope. It is the global, not the local, so it is a copy, and set()
# writes through it. On main colm took it for the local, and the program
# segfaulted in set().
def d
	I: int
	[]
void set( X: ref<d> ) { X.I = 9 }
namespace a
	global G: d = cons d[]
end
int t()
{
	G: d = cons d[]
	G.I = 100
	set( a::G )
	print( G.I, "\n" )
	return 0
}
t()
##### COMP_ERR #####
16:2: set can write through ref parameter X, so arg 1 must be a local, or an attribute or child of one
